{
  "chapter": "STARTING_OUT_WITH_LINES",
  "description": "§aSilicone Rubber§r is one of two primary rubber types utilized for §bIV and higher-tier cables§r. While its full production chain involves a multi-step process, the final step needs you to react §eMethanol§r with §eSilicon Dust§r within a §bChemical Reactor§r.

This material is critically required for the creation of various §dLuV Components§r in the GregTech assembly line, making its production mandatory for your progression.

Compared to §aStyrene Butadiene Rubber§r, §aSilicone Rubber§r is generally §6easier to produce§r. While it offers §6lesser performance for cable recipes§r, its necessity for specific components means it cannot be bypassed, unlike §aStyrene Butadiene Rubber§r which can technically be substituted in some applications.

§r§o§6For a complete overview of the Silicone Rubber production system, consult EMI/JEI for detailed recipes and processes.§r",
